HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The kkpprroocc__ssttaarrtt() function first appeared in FreeBSD 2.2.  The
     kkpprroocc__sshhuuttddoowwnn(), kkpprroocc__ccrreeaattee(), kkpprroocc__eexxiitt(), kkpprroocc__rreessuummee(),
     kkpprroocc__ssuussppeenndd(), and kkpprroocc__ssuussppeenndd__cchheecckk() functions were introduced in
     FreeBSD 4.0.  Prior to FreeBSD 5.0, the kkpprroocc__sshhuuttddoowwnn(), kkpprroocc__rreessuummee(),
     kkpprroocc__ssuussppeenndd(), and kkpprroocc__ssuussppeenndd__cchheecckk() functions were named
     sshhuuttddoowwnn__kkpprroocc(), rreessuummee__kkpprroocc(), sshhuuttddoowwnn__kkpprroocc(), and
     kkpprroocc__ssuussppeenndd__lloooopp(), respectively.  Originally they had the names
     kktthhrreeaadd__**() but were changed to kkpprroocc__**() when real kthreads became
     available.

